        '6-8', $q$Draft: The Ice Harvest$q$, $q$(1) Before electric refrigerators, families kept food cold with ice cut from frozen ponds, and Tomas Ferreira's article "When Ice Came from Ponds" explains how this work was done. (2) ____. (3) Ferreira describes workers sawing the pond ice into blocks that weighed about one hundred pounds each. (4) The blocks were then floated along open channels in the ice to an icehouse beside the shore. (5) Ferreira writes that "a skilled crew could cut and store two thousand blocks in a single day." (6) This number shows that ice harvesting took careful teamwork, not just strong arms.

(7) The ice also had to last all summer. (8) Ferreira explains that workers packed the blocks in thick layers of sawdust, which kept warm air away from the ice. (9) Ice is frozen water. (10) Because of this packing, much of the ice stayed frozen until late August. (11) Ferreira's details show that ____.$q$, 'draft')
