   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (4) to explain the quotation in sentence 3?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This detail shows that Rosa should quit the swim team and try a different sport.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"This detail shows that sprinting early left Rosa too tired to finish the race strongly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"This detail shows that sand can be found at the bottom of many lakes and rivers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"This detail shows that Rosa's arms were wet because she was swimming in a pool.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$This detail shows that sprinting early left Rosa too tired to finish the race strongly.$q$, $q$Saying her arms "felt like wet sand" means they felt heavy and tired, which shows the cost of sprinting early. Reading it as her arms simply being wet misses what the comparison means.$q$, 'draft', '0d44d488-c958-5083-8b9b-f1803d3da879')
