   $q$The writer wants to add a quotation after sentence 7 to show that Rosa used her coach's advice. Which quotation works best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Okafor writes that the pool \"smelled of chlorine and somebody's sunscreen.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-evidence"},{"text":"Okafor writes that the rival team wore \"bright orange suits that matched.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-evidence"},{"text":"Okafor writes that Rosa \"counted each stroke, just the way Mr. Halvorsen had shown her.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"Okafor writes that Rosa \"wanted to win more than she wanted anything.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"does-not-show-change"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Okafor writes that Rosa "counted each stroke, just the way Mr. Halvorsen had shown her."$q$, $q$Counting strokes is exactly what the coach taught in sentence 5, so this quotation proves Rosa used his advice. Wanting to win shows her goal but not that she changed how she swims.$q$, 'draft', '0d44d488-c958-5083-8b9b-f1803d3da879')
