-- Passage wg7-writing-with-evidence-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('db32e9c7-e803-5ade-877f-b477ea42993f', 'wg7-writing-with-evidence-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: Hands from a Printer$q$, $q$(1) In "Hands from a Printer," Kenji Mori writes about a group of volunteers who use 3D printers to make plastic hands for children. (2) Mori shows that these printed hands help children because they are cheap, easy to replace, and fun to design. (3) Mori explains that a regular artificial hand can cost thousands of dollars, while a printed one costs about fifty dollars in plastic. (4) ____ children grow quickly and often need a new hand every year. (5) Mori writes that "when a child outgrows a printed hand, the volunteers simply print a bigger one." (6) The low cost makes it possible for families to replace the hand as often as needed.

(7) The children also help design their own hands. (8) Mori describes a girl named Ana who asked for a hand with purple fingers and silver stars. (9) According to Mori, children who choose their own colors are more likely to wear their hands every day. (10) 3D printers can also make toys, phone cases, and bike parts. (11) In the end, the printed hands are good.$q$, 'draft')
