   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence 7 to explain Grandpa's words. Which sentence works best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Grandpa's joke shows that Darnell will never be able to learn the song.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Grandpa's joke shows that he is patient and wants Darnell to keep trying instead of giving up.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Grandpa's joke shows that he was a poor musician for his whole life.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Grandpa's joke shows that the steel pan is very hard to keep in tune.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Grandpa's joke shows that he is patient and wants Darnell to keep trying instead of giving up.$q$, $q$Grandpa laughs and compares Darnell's mistakes to his own early ones, which encourages Darnell to keep going. Taking the joke to mean Grandpa was always a poor musician ignores that he plays the song every evening.$q$, 'draft', '32c27476-9174-52e9-8910-68cf08a3b31b')
