   $q$Which explanation best shows how the quotation in sentence 8 supports the draft's claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the two of them played so loudly that no one could hear the notes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows that summer is the best season for anyone to learn a new instrument.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"It shows that Grandpa stopped playing the song once Darnell learned it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows that Darnell and Grandpa now play as equals, so the old song has joined them together.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that Darnell and Grandpa now play as equals, so the old song has joined them together.$q$, $q$When "nobody could tell whose notes were whose," the boy and his grandfather sound like one player, which shows the music has brought them close. The quotation says they played side by side, so Grandpa did not stop playing.$q$, 'draft', '32c27476-9174-52e9-8910-68cf08a3b31b')
