insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1971d341-5ee0-5d6e-97b8-40807ee701fe', 'wg7-writing-with-evidence-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: How Octopuses Hide$q$, $q$(1) In the article "Masters of Disguise," Ines Alvarado explains how octopuses hide from the animals that hunt them. (2) Alvarado shows that octopuses survive by changing both their color and their shape. (3) She explains that an octopus's skin contains thousands of tiny color cells that can open or close in less than a second. (4) Alvarado writes that "an octopus resting on a spotted rock can turn spotted before a fish swims past." (5) This shows that ____.

(6) Color is not the octopus's only trick. (7) Alvarado describes how an octopus can raise small bumps on its skin so it looks like rough coral or seaweed. (8) One kind of octopus can even stretch out its arms and drift like a loose strand of seaweed. (9) I think octopuses are the smartest animals in the whole ocean. (10) Because octopuses have no hard shell to protect them, these disguises are their main defense.$q$, 'draft')
